# What `plow-agents mint` writes. Copying this and filling it in by hand works
# too, if you already hold an agent credential -- but then `revoke` has no key
# id to read, and you revoke it in the Plow dashboard instead.
#
# Mode 600: it is a bearer token, and it names the API that token is sent to.
# So copy it with the mode, not with `cp` -- `cp` would hand the copy this
# file's world-readable one:
#
#     install -m 600 plow-credentials.example plow-credentials
#
# `mint` records the key id here as a comment, because the image accepts exactly
# the two names below and a third NAME=value line is a refused boot. No such
# line here on purpose: an id that is not yours reads to `revoke` as a key Plow
# has already forgotten, so it would delete this file with your token still live.

# The Plow API root, WITHOUT /v1 -- the agent appends its own.
PLOW_API_BASE=https://api.plow.co
# The agent's own credential: that line's chats, Plow's inference, `relay:call`,
# and `payments:request` with a $200/day cap. The last two reach past the
# container -- onto the owner's own machine, and onto the owner's card. See the README.
PLOW_AGENT_TOKEN=
